(1786, 245, 'Which association measure filters out trivial correlations?', 'Lift', 'Support alone', 'The number of items', 'The transaction count', 'A', 'Lift measures the strength of association beyond chance.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(1787, 245, 'In Apriori, candidate generation creates itemsets of size:', 'One larger than the previous frequent level', 'The same size', 'Any random size', 'Double the size', 'A', 'Candidates of size k+1 are generated from frequent k-itemsets.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(1788, 245, 'Which clustering method uses a dissimilarity matrix and agglomerative merging?', 'Hierarchical agglomerative clustering', 'k-means', 'Apriori', 'Linear regression', 'A', 'Agglomerative methods merge the closest clusters step by step.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(1789, 245, 'What is the purpose of the minimum confidence threshold?', 'To filter rules that are not reliable enough', 'To limit data size', 'To choose k', 'To select features', 'A', 'Only rules above the confidence threshold are reported.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(1790, 245, 'Which is a drawback of k-means?', 'It requires choosing k in advance', 'It needs labeled data', 'It cannot handle numbers', 'It finds no clusters', 'A', 'k must be specified, and results depend on initialization.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(1791, 245, 'What is the main scalability challenge of the classic Apriori algorithm?', 'It scans the database repeatedly for large candidate sets', 'It uses too little memory', 'It has no candidates', 'It never prunes', 'A', 'Multiple scans and candidate generation limit Apriori''s scalability.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(1792, 245, 'Which alternative to Apriori avoids generating candidates explicitly?', 'FP-Growth using a frequent-pattern tree', 'Apriori itself', 'k-means', 'Decision trees', 'A', 'FP-Growth compresses data in an FP-tree and mines without candidate generation.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
